text:
maya: Quick accessibility pass on the activity models list and compact row actions. Found some keyboard/focus oddities and a couple of SR (screen reader) surprises. Posting notes.

sam: Thanks. Short repro? I can run through locally.

maya: Steps I hit on staging: Tab into list, use ArrowDown to move, press Enter on a row to open the right flyout, press Esc. Expected: focus returns to the activating row. Observed: focus lands on the page header or sometimes the hidden skiplink element.

ravi: I see this too. Also NVDA reads "Open, button, collapsed" when it's just an expand toggle 1 That double state read seems caused by both visible text and aria-expanded on a child element.

maya: Another one: the small action chips (rename, copy, delete) are using 10px text + low contrast gray. Fails AA for body text. In dark theme the delete chip is almost invisible unless hovered.

toni: Two likely culprits: (1) we render an offscreen focus trap div that retains tabindex when flyout closes; (2) we have duplicate ARIA labels on the toggle (visible label + aria-label on inner icon).

toni: Proposed quick fixes: ensure trap div tabindex is removed/changed to -1 when hidden; change toggle markup to single accessible label; on close, if the trigger element still exists, call trigger.focus({preventScroll:true}); if it was removed, move focus to the next logical control (first toolbar button).

sam: Pseudocode I'll use in PR:

```javascript
// close handler
function handleClose(triggerId) {
  const trigger = document.getElementById(triggerId);
  flyout.setAttribute('aria-hidden','true');
  trapDiv.tabIndex = -1;
  if (trigger && document.contains(trigger)) {
    trigger.focus({preventScroll:true});
  } else {
    document.querySelector('.toolbar .btn-primary').focus();
  }
}
```

maya: Nice. Can we also strengthen the focus halo for small controls? Current 2px light ring disappears on dark card backgrounds. Suggest 3px with a slightly darker outline color.

a11y-bot: Auto-report: 4 issues found on /models page (sample):
- color: `.chip` (#A3A3A3 on #0B0F13) fails AA at 12px. Suggest #C7C7C7 or update token `chip-muted`.
- semantics: `.row-toggle > span[aria-label]` duplicates visible text -> SR repeats. Remove aria-label when visible text present.
- tab order: hidden focus trap uses tabindex="0" when flyout closed. Should be tabindex="-1" or aria-hidden.
- announcements: toast stack uses role="status" but has aria-live="polite" on each; multiple polite regions cause delayed announcements. Recommend single live region and queue messages.

ravi: I'll run NVDA/VoiceOver matrix after PR. My test plan: keyboard-only flow, screen reader focus trail, and a11y smoke in dark/light. Will note if Escape should close flyout and announce 'Closed model details for <name>'.

sam: I'll also audit markup for role misuse (div role=button) and ensure interactive elements are real buttons/anchors.

maya: Copy nit: toggle buttons say "Open" visually and we have aria-pressed on the same element -> VoiceOver reads "Open button pressed" which is confusing. Use `aria-expanded` for disclosure toggles and `aria-pressed` only for toggles that persist state.

toni: I'll update token file for chip/disabled colors and push a small visual regression. Also will add a keyboard utility to centralize focus restore patterns.

sam: PR drafted, includes: focus restore, trap tabindex fix, remove duplicate aria-labels, change row markup to `button` for toggle, and focus halo update. Will tag @ravi for validation.

maya: Awesome. After Ravi verifies, I'll paste an acceptance checklist into the PR: tab order, esc closes, focus restore, announcement text, contrast check light/dark, NVDA + VoiceOver passes.

a11y-bot: Note: after fixes run automated check again to catch remaining contrast and duplicate-label issues.

ravi: I'll watch for the PR and run the matrix. Thanks everyone. :thumbsup:

maya: End-to-end goal: keyboard-first flows in the models list feel predictable; no duplicate SR labels; visible focus states in both themes. Minimal UX disruption.

sam: Will ping here when PR is live.
